# Dr Brain - Motor Programming — LLM Guide

Dr Brain - Motor Programming (the first game in the Dr Brain collection) is a robot programming puzzle for humans and AI agents. A robot stands on a grid with
rocks and treats. You fill a main tape and a few subroutine tapes with instructions; the robot
runs them one step at a time. Collect every treat to win.

Humans: open {{.BaseURL}}/ , pick a map and press Run. Tutorial: {{.BaseURL}}/learn
Spectate a session live: {{.BaseURL}}/watch/SESSION_ID

GraphQL endpoint:       POST {{.BaseURL}}/graphql
GraphQL subscriptions:  {{.WSURL}}/graphql  (graphql-ws protocol)
Playground:             GET  {{.BaseURL}}/playground
Introspection:          enabled unless the operator disabled it — query __schema/__type

Every example below is valid against the live schema. Replace SESSION_ID with an id returned by
createSession and MAP_ID with an id from the `maps` query.

---

## Rules

- A session is one run of one map. The map is snapshotted when the session is created.
- A program is one `main` tape plus N `subs` tapes. Tape lengths are fixed per map
  (`mainTapeLength`, `subTapeLengths`); `setProgram` requires exactly those lengths. Pad with
  EMPTY.
- Execution is one instruction per step. EMPTY slots are skipped for free (not a step). When a
  sub tape ends, control returns to the caller. When the main tape ends the program is over.
- The robot wins the moment the last treat is collected (a win beats the step limit on the same
  step). Otherwise it loses with a `lossReason`:
  - STEP_LIMIT      — `steps` reached the map's `maxSteps`
  - CALL_DEPTH      — more than `maxCallDepth` calls in flight
  - PROGRAM_ENDED   — main tape finished with treats left
- MOVE_FORWARD into a rock or off the map is a silent no-op (still a step, `blocked: true`).
- Collecting happens on arrival; the start cell never holds a treat.
- A CALL_SUB_k that targets an already active sub (or one anywhere on the call stack) does
  nothing (still counts as a step) unless the map has `allowRecursion: true`.
- `setProgram` and `reset` put the robot back at the start. `setProgram` is rejected while the
  session is playing (`SESSION_PLAYING`). Terminal sessions (WON/LOST) refuse run/step until
  `reset` (`SESSION_TERMINAL`).

### Instructions

| value        | effect                                             |
|--------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| EMPTY        | skipped, costs nothing                             |
| TURN_LEFT    | rotate 90 degrees counter-clockwise                |
| TURN_RIGHT   | rotate 90 degrees clockwise                        |
| MOVE_FORWARD | move one cell in the facing direction              |
| CALL_SUB_1   | run subroutine tape 1 (`subs[0]`), then come back  |
| CALL_SUB_2   | run subroutine tape 2 (`subs[1]`)                  |
| CALL_SUB_3   | run subroutine tape 3 (`subs[2]`)                  |

CALL_SUB_k is only valid when the map has at least k sub tapes.

### Coordinates

- `x` is the column, `y` is the row. Row 0 is the TOP row of `layout`; `y` grows DOWNWARD.
- Facing: UP = y-1, RIGHT = x+1, DOWN = y+1, LEFT = x-1.
- `layout` glyphs: `.` empty, `#` rock, `*` treat, `^ > v <` start cell and initial facing.
- Frame `tape: -1` is the main tape; `pc` is the index of the next instruction on that tape.
  The last entry of `callStack` is the active tape.

### Errors

Errors carry `extensions.code`: NOT_FOUND, INVALID_PROGRAM, SESSION_PLAYING, SESSION_TERMINAL,
INVALID_ARGUMENT, FORBIDDEN, LIMIT_REACHED. Admin mutations need an `X-Admin-Key` header.

